{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\nWritable container layers are each container's overlay2 `upperdir`. They grow independently of\nimage layers and build cache, no prune reaches them, and nothing measured them on 2026-09-02 —\nthe only signal was \"root disk high\". Last cap under ADR 0112.\n\n## Mechanism decision, with evidence\nThe ticket offers a runtime storage quota \"when compatible\", else a reaper. **The quota is NOT\ncompatible here.** overlay2's `--storage-opt size=` (and the `overlay2.size` daemon default) is\naccepted only when the filesystem backing `/var/lib/docker` is XFS mounted with `pquota`, else\nthe daemon refuses: `--storage-opt is supported only for overlay over xfs with 'pquota' mount\noption`. That filesystem is ROOT here, and XFS reads quota options at MOUNT time and refuses\nthem on a remount — so it needs `rootflags=pquota` and a REBOOT: the constraint S4 (`2ba3`) hit\nfor `/var/tmp`. Even after that reboot it is PER-CONTAINER, not an aggregate ceiling, and\napplies at creation, so every live service must be recreated. So this ships the mitigation,\npublishes which regime the box is in, and documents how to enable it.\n\n## What the reaper does NOT guarantee\n1. **It cannot reclaim a RUNNING container's writable layer at all.** Only exited/dead ones are\n   removable, so for the live compose set this is MEASUREMENT AND AN ALARM, not a bound; only\n   the reboot-gated quota would bound those. Sharper than S4's fill rate, so it is said first.\n2. For the debris it does bound, the bound is `cap + fill_rate x interval`: at 2 GiB and 300 s a\n   sustained net fill above ~7.2 MB/s outruns it, and this gp3 volume does 125 MB/s (~17x).\n3. Nothing that exited inside the 900 s grace window is removed. When it cannot get under the\n   share it SAYS SO.\n\n## Safety — proved against the live set\n`docker container prune --filter until=…` cannot express what this host needs: its filters are\n`until` and `label` only, with NO name filter. `autodeploy.sh` starts the mcp blue-green\nbackends with a bare `docker run` compose never sees, and reaps them in `mcp_retire_sweep` under\na guard this reaper cannot replicate — it reads the nginx `/mcp/` upstream include and refuses\nto reap an exited container still named as the live backend, since `--restart always` would have\nrestored it. Reaping one anyway is bug `9ea3`: a transient exit became a permanent 502 on\n2026-09-02. So candidates are removed one by one, sparing:\n\n* `com.docker.compose.project`-labelled (gerrit, review-bot, opcert, compose-mcp-1): an exited\n  compose service is a crashed one whose logs are the evidence;\n* `rebar.service`-labelled (`mcp_run_new`'s stable identity);\n* matching `^(rebar-mcp|compose-mcp-1)` — `mcp_managed`'s regex, so the two agree.\n\nTwo daemon-enforced guarantees, not shell logic: candidates come from `docker ps -a --filter\nstatus=exited --filter status=dead`, which never lists a running container; removal is\n`docker rm` WITHOUT `-f`, which the daemon refuses for a running one (the `mcp_retire_image`\nprecedent). No `-v`/`--volumes`; `docker system prune` never used.\n\n**Sizes and termination.** ONE `docker inspect --size` over every container gives the total and\neach candidate's `SizeRw` — the same field `docker system df` sums into its Containers row, so\ncensus and ledger cannot disagree. The loop sorts by `State.FinishedAt` ASCENDING (oldest exit\nfirst) and SUBTRACTS each removed container's size from its running total, stopping at 80% of\nthe share; it never re-reads the ledger per removal, which would be N daemon walks that could\nnot converge while other containers are still writing.\n\n## What invokes the reaper, and what publishes the heartbeat\nTwo DIFFERENT callers; naming one is how a heartbeat ends up with no producer. The REAPER runs\nfrom its own `rebar-container-reaper.timer` (5 min, `TimeoutStartSec` nested strictly below the\nperiod per bug `1205`), rendered by `--print-units` and installed by `compose-up.sh` beside the\nthree caps it already installs — a timer rather than an autodeploy hook, since\n`prune_docker_caches` runs only on deploy/backoff/pressure paths. The HEARTBEAT comes from\n`observability.sh`'s existing 5-minute timer (`install-observability.sh`), whose §2i calls the\nside-effect-free `--check-active`. So \"every tick\" is the OBSERVABILITY tick, and the heartbeat\nstill has a producer when the reaper timer is the dead thing — the point of it.\n\n## Observability (S2's publish-or-stay-silent rule)\n§2i, from the SAME single `docker system df` call §2f already makes — the format string gains\n`{{.Reclaimable}}` rather than a second daemon walk: `container_writable_bytes` (Containers\nSize), `container_exited_bytes` (Containers Reclaimable), `container_writable_used_percent`\n(`pct_of_cap`, S3's helper, reused), plus two 1/0 ALWAYS-PUBLISH STATE METRICS:\n`container_reaper_active` (is the timer in force — the heartbeat) and\n`container_quota_enforceable` (is the kernel enforcing XFS project quota on the Docker root fs,\nso could a ceiling exist). Those two publish on EVERY tick including their 0 path; the three\ndf-derived readings above publish ONLY on a parseable Containers row.\n\n**Field surface verified — MATCH** against the CLI reference: `docker system df --format`\nexposes `{{.Reclaimable}}`, and on the Containers row `Size` sums writable layers (`SizeRw`)\nwhile `Reclaimable` is the non-running subset. An unrecognised row or missing third field\npublishes NOTHING, so a rendering change degrades to silence.\n\n## Alarms (`monitoring_autodeploy.tf`)\n`rebar-container-writable-usage-high` (>85%) and `rebar-container-reaper-not-active` (<1).\n**The second pre-empts the S4 finding**: without it a silently-dead timer leaves usage nominal\nwhile nothing enforces anything. Both `treat_missing_data = \"breaching\"`, both SNS-wired.\n`container_quota_enforceable` gets NO alarm: it reads 0 until the reboot, and a permanently\nfiring alarm is muted within a day.\n\n## Which file owns what\n`docker-storage-cap.sh` owns the BUDGET; `container-cap.sh` owns the reaper, the checks and the\nrendering. ADR 0112 puts this share INSIDE the Docker budget, so `docker-storage-cap.sh` gains\n`DOCKER_CONTAINER_WRITABLE_BYTES` (2 GiB) carved out of the existing 20 GiB: BuildKit 5 + this 2\n+ images 13 = 20 GiB, images having been 15. `container-cap.sh` READS it, so no second literal\ndrifts. The 2 GiB is an ADR 0112 decision-6 starting point: no writable-layer figure was\ncaptured at the outage.\n\n## Scope\nIn, enumerated: NEW `infra/scripts/container-cap.sh`; `docker-storage-cap.sh` (third share);\n`observability.sh` (§2i + extended parse); `compose-up.sh` (installs the timer);\n`infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf`; `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`;\n`tests/scripts/test_docker_storage_cap.py` (its `DOCKER_IMAGE_SHARE_BYTES` assertions move to\nthe three-way split); `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py`; two NEW test files.\nOut: overlay2 deletion, S2/S3/S4's caps, gate scratch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `--reap` removes an exited unowned container over the share, nothing under it (tested at\n      90% of the share, between the low-water mark and the ceiling), reaps oldest-first to the\n      80% mark, and WARNs naming the running and protected bytes when it cannot get under.\n- [ ] `--reap` removes nothing for each of: a `running` row; a `com.docker.compose.project`\n      label; a `rebar.service` label; a `rebar-mcp-*` / `compose-mcp-1` name; an exit inside the\n      grace window; an unreadable share. Its argv never contains `-f`, `-v`, `--volumes`,\n      `system prune` or `container prune`. A test pins the name pattern to `mcp_managed`'s.\n\n- [ ] `observability.sh` publishes the three df-derived readings from a parseable Containers row\n      and NONE when absent or unparseable; percent clamped to 100; the two state metrics publish\n      every tick including their 0 path; all five dimensionless.\n- [ ] `docker-storage-cap.sh --print-env` states the third share, the three sum to the budget\n      (5+2+13=20 GiB), and an over-subscribed split is refused.\n- [ ] Both alarms exist by name, `treat_missing_data = \"breaching\"`, SNS-wired, asserted in\n      `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py`; `terraform fmt -check`/`validate` pass.\n\n- [ ] The runbook documents diagnosis, remediation, the `rootflags=pquota` + reboot steps, and\n      forbids manual overlay2 deletion.\n\n- [ ] Portability: Docker APIs, systemd and local pytest only; no CI-provider trigger."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788595084224086001,"uuid":"a0edc9f9-5b21-45a4-b13a-7fc808b8cb5e"}